          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            9. BulkSupplements vs Nutricost and Naked: Which Is the Better Buy?
          </h2>

          <p>
            BulkSupplements is about as cheap as Nutricost for casein and cheaper than Naked, but it is the barest of the three. Nutricost's 5 lb unflavored casein, at the $74.95 Amazon price we saw, gives 25 g of protein per 35 g scoop per its label, which by weight is about 65 servings and about $1.16 per 25 g. BulkSupplements' 1 kg casein lands at about $1.18, practically the same.
          </p>

          <p>
            Where Nutricost wins is convenience. It sells casein in flavored versions as well as unflavored, ships in a tub with a scoop rather than a pouch, and offers one big 5 lb container instead of making you choose between 1 kg and 5 kg bags. Our <a href="/nutricost-protein-powder-review/">Nutricost protein powder review</a> covers its testing claims and full range. If you hate the taste of plain casein, Nutricost's chocolate or vanilla is the easier switch at a similar price per gram.
          </p>

          <p>
            Naked Casein is the premium unflavored alternative. Its 1 lb bag was $29.99 on Amazon when we checked, with 15 servings of about 26 g of protein per the brand, which is about $1.92 per 25 g. For that extra money you get a product Naked promotes as NSF Certified, a brand that leans heavily on sourcing claims, and a smaller bag. See our <a href="/naked-nutrition-protein-powder-review/">Naked Nutrition review</a> for its label details.
          </p>

          <p>
            The short version: pick BulkSupplements when you want the lowest price on a single-ingredient powder and will flavor it yourself; pick Nutricost if you want the same price with flavor options and a tub; pick Naked if you want a certification claim on an unflavored casein and will pay about 60 percent more for it. For product-by-product matchups across the site, browse the <a href="/protein-powder-comparison/">protein powder comparisons</a> index.
          </p>
